 translations","Terms with Punjabi translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Samoan translations","Terms with Serbo-Croatian translations","Terms with Sindhi translations","Terms with Sinhalese translations","Terms with Slovak translations","Terms with Somali translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Swahili translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Tagalog translations","Terms with Tamil translations","Terms with Telugu translations","Terms with Thai translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Terms with Urdu translations","Terms with Uzbek translations","Terms with Welsh translations","Terms with Yiddish translations","en:Automobiles"],"links":[["dilapidated","dilapidated"],["unpretentious","unpretentious"],["automobile","automobile"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"banger"},{"word":"beater"},{"word":"banger","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["UK"]},{"word":"beater","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"bucket of bolts","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"bucket of rust","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"clunker","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"crate","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"crock","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["UK"]},{"word":"flivver","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["Canada","US","dated"]},{"word":"hooptie","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"jalopy","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["US","dated"]},{"word":"junker","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["Canada","US"]},{"word":"lemon","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"old banger","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["UK"]},{"word":"rattletrap","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"rustbucket","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"shed","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["UK"]},{"word":"shitbox","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["vulgar"]},{"word":"shitpot","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["vulgar"]},{"word":"shitcan","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["vulgar"]},{"word":"shitbucket","source":"Thesaurus:old car","tags":["vulgar"]},{"word":"tin Lizzie","source":"Thesaurus:old car"},{"word":"wreck","source":"Thesaurus:old car"}],"raw_glosses":["(US, dated) An old, dilapidated or unpretentious automobile."],"glosses":["An old, dilapidated or unpretentious automobile."],"tags":["US","dated"],"wikipedia":["Michael Quinion"],"id":"ed0c4da4-33a0-402b-a82c-5d4f3cd7d927"}],"related":[{"tags":["possibly"],"word":"jalapeño"}],"synonyms":[]},"jalousie":{"id":"61d7859c-7c70-4c09-8bf9-e54a495ffe16","word":"jalousie","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"window slats which form a blind or shutter","tags":["feminine"],"word":"gelosia"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"topics":["architecture","government","military","naval","navy","politics","war"],"links":[["ventilation","ventilation"]],"raw_glosses":["(naval architecture) A component in a ventilation system."],"glosses":["A component in a ventilation system."],"id":"3c1b3f08-6aab-4fab-afe7-814a535e1980"},{"examples":[{"text":"A small lofty room, with its window wide open, and the wooden jalousie-blinds closed, so that the dark night only showed in slight horizontal lines of black, alternating with their broad lines of stone colour.","ref":"1859, Charles Dickens, A Tale of Two Cities:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[62,70]],"id":"7b735f04-54cd-4ca1-8bdf-f699779cb638"},{"text":"Nowhere the glitter of a glass casement; Venetian blinds, jalousies, closed every window, and rooms projected in all directions to catch the luxury of a through-draft of air.","ref":"2014, Kate Pullinger, The Last Time I Saw Jane:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[58,67]],"id":"43ea17e1-5b18-4f29-9d37-2854c5c1696d"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Upward sloping window slats which form a blind or shutter, allowing light and air in but excluding rain and direct sun."],"id":"32aeff0f-6806-45ff-921b-41731d269fff"},{"links":[["pastry","pastry"]],"glosses":["A pastry with the upper side sliced before final baking to resemble a wooden slatted blind."],"id":"ac4ac3fa-7ae3-403f-9857-60a45ea8e6e7"}],"related":[{"word":"blind"},{"word":"curtain"}],"synonyms":[]},"Jalalabad":{"id":"5ec86b74-bd13-40a5-af46-1e35cc272ee8","word":"Jalalabad","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a city in eastern Afghanistan","word":"Jalalabad"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"wikidata":["Q183303"],"senseid":["en:Q183303"],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English proper nouns","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Korean terms with redundant transliterations","Pages with 2 entries","Pages with entries","Requests for pronunciation in English entries","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Bishnupriya Manipuri translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Estonian translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Hindi translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Korean translations","Terms with Lithuanian translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Marathi translations","Terms with Newar translations","Terms with Norwegian translations","Terms with Pashto translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Tajik translations","Terms with Turkish translations","en:Cities in Afghanistan","en:Places in Afghanistan","en:Provincial capitals of Afghanistan"],"links":[["capital city","capital city"],["Nangarhar","Nangarhar#English"],["Afghanistan","Afghanistan#English"]],"glosses":["The capital city of Nangarhar province, Afghanistan."],"id":"42624355-35dc-42dc-94c1-34291bd91ad5"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"jalebi":{"id":"b284f4f7-5706-4756-81dd-7926fd350c32","word":"jalebi","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Translations","word":"jalebi"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"You will not believe how quickly jalebis can be made. I have used yeast to ferment the jalebi batter quickly and so it does not require to be left for a day to ferment. The trick here is to immediately start frying the jalebis once the batter has rested for 10 minutes.","ref":"2000, Tarla Dalal, Chaat, page 98:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[33,39],[33,40],[87,93],[219,225],[219,226]],"id":"174bc3b6-d9d5-4c17-a180-abfcd730b032"},{"text":"On the way he saw a sweetmeat seller making jalebis (spiral sweet). He was tempted. In his mind he thought he'd have some jalebis.","ref":"2001, B.S. Rana, Jataka Tales, page 80:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[44,51],[122,129]],"id":"cb283039-3c5c-440b-b628-0302e536ccef"},{"text":"But Bhole refused to listen. He became very angry and started to scream, “I want jalebis! Give me jalebis! I want them now!”","ref":"2006, Hema De Munnikl, Bhole: Adventures of a Young Yogi, page 22:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[81,88],[98,105]],"id":"1b0f6807-3414-4bdb-a714-62991bfba72d"},{"text":"Mr. Alam and his staff often insist that visitors enjoy a free treat like chocolate barfi, condensed milk mixed with chocolate, or jalebis, deep fried rice flour coated in a sugary syrup, while they shop. “I want my customers to feel welcome and offering mithai is a way to show hospitality,” Mr. Alam said.","ref":"2018 January 17, Shivani Vora, “A Go-To Grocery for Indian Cooks”, in The New York Times, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[131,138]],"id":"bbdb5e9c-8f06-48b0-948b-498dec0b5aaf"}],"links":[["sweet","sweet"],["Indian","Indian"],["subcontinent","subcontinent"],["deep-fry","deep-fry"],["maida","maida"],["flour","flour"],["batter","batt